ZyperOS: three VFPU operations compiled by the ARM64 JIT instead of handed to the interpreter, from
Deadstation Portable (github.com/tyrannotorus/emulator-deadstation-portable, GPL-2.0-or-later as PPSSPP),
a PPSSPP v1.20.4 fork for the TrimUI Brick: its commit c0877a2 (vsge, vslt) and its first
commit fbde7d6 (vf2i, and vsin, vcos and vasin of one value).

The interpreter's way costs a full register flush, its generic vector reads and writes and its
prefix handling around one instruction. Each case is the interpreter's arithmetic, bit for bit:
- vsge, vslt: FCMP, CSET, UCVTF a lane; a NaN gives 0.0 (an unordered compare sets neither GE nor
  MI); a lane whose S or T swizzle reads past the vector is 0.0 (RetainInvalidSwizzleST)
- vf2i without prefixes: the scale is a power of two (exact), its overflow to infinity saturates as
  Int_Vf2i's caps do, the conversion rounds as the instruction says (n, z, u, d), NaN 0x7FFFFFFF
- vsin, vcos, vasin of a single value without prefixes: the interpreter's own function on the same
  value in the same rounding mode, called directly

